{
  "summary": "This review examines strategies to redirect lipid nanoparticles (LNPs) for extrahepatic RNA delivery, addressing challenges like hepatotropism and limited cell specificity. It evaluates formulation chemistry, surface engineering, and administration routes to achieve tissue-specific targeting in organs such as spleen, lungs, and tumors. The study highlights key determinants of LNP tropism and clinical translation pathways while identifying major challenges in biodistribution and safety.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Conventional LNPs exhibit intrinsic hepatotropism limiting extrahepatic RNA delivery",
    "Surface functionalization and lipid chemistry modifications enable tissue-specific LNP targeting",
    "Clinical translation faces challenges including cell-resolved biodistribution and repeated-dose immunogenicity"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a systematic framework for optimizing LNP design to achieve precise extrahep:atic RNA delivery, advancing the therapeutic potential of RNA medicines beyond hepatic applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluates a c-Met-targeting aptamer-drug conjugate (SL1-MMAE) for treating primary and metastatic uveal melanoma. In vitro and in vivo models demonstrated potent tumor suppression, significant survival prolongation, and robust intraocular tumor regression with minimal ocular toxicity after intravitreal injection. The ApDC's small size enabled superior tumor penetration and reduced off-target effects, showing advantages over clinical ADCs for intraocular delivery.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SL1-Musing the c-Met-targeting aptamer-drug conjugate suppressed tumor growth in subcutaneous and liver metastasis models",
    "A single intravitreal injection of SL1-MMAE induced tumor regression in orthotopic intraocular models without ocular toxicity",
    "The ApDC demonstrated superior antitumor efficacy and ocular biocompatibility compared to the clinical ADC ABBV-399"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes c-Met-targeting aptamer-drug conjugates as a viable platform for vision-preserving therapy in uveal melanoma, leveraging targeted delivery and reduced ocular toxicity for both primary and metastatic disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study describes the BICAN's basal ganglia atlas, a collaborative effort to create a reference map integrating cell identities, anatomy, and multimodal data across species. It aims to advance understanding of brain organization, function, variation, and disease through a federated reference model inspired by the Human Genome Project.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Integration of cell identities, anatomy, and multimodal evidence across species",
    "Development of a federated reference model for brain organization and function",
    "Foundation for understanding brain variation and disease mechanisms"
  ],
  "study_type": "Collaborative atlas project",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable framework for cross-species brain reference mapping, providing a foundational resource for neuroscience research on brain structure and function."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a synchronic multilevel assembly strategy to synthesize mesoporous intercalation-type metal oxide frameworks for fast-charging sodium-ion batteries. By atomic-scale cation assembly and in situ conductive carbon integration, the researchers developed sodium titanate composites with enhanced rate capability (∼115 mAh g⁻¹ at 10 A g⁻¹) and cycling stability (<0.023% fade per 1000 cycles). The findings demonstrate ultrafast sodium diffusion pathways enabling high-rate performance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Synchronic multilevel assembly enables structurally tunable mesoporous sodium titanate anodes",
    "M-Na4Ti5O12/C composite achieves ∼115 mAh g⁻¹ at 10 A g⁻¹ with minimal capacity fade",
    "Interconnected mesoporous channels facilitate ultrafast Na+ diffusion for high-rate cycling"
  ],
  "study_type": "Synthetic strategy",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a rational design framework for developing high-rate sodium-ion battery anodes through structural engineering of mesoporous frameworks."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered a ternary polysaccharide-polyaniline nanocomplex (CFP) to enhance near-infrared photothermal therapy. The CFP complex, formed via curdlan's hydrophobic cavity, improved polyaniline dispersion and stability while fucoidan suppressed pyrimidine metabolism. Multi-omics analysis showed downregulation of key pyrimidine enzymes, impairing DNA repair and synergistically enhancing tumor ablation with minimal toxicity in mice.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CFP nanocomplexes improve polyaniline dispersion and stability via curdlan's hydrophobic cavity",
    "Fucoidan suppresses pyrimidine metabolism by downregulating TK1, DTYMK, and CDA",
    "Synergistic photothermal tumor ablation with reduced DNA repair capacity and minimal toxicity in mice"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies in immunocompetent mice",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a strategy for metabolic reprogramming via natural polysaccharides to enhance photothermal therapy efficacy while maintaining systemic biosafety."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrates single-cell multiomic profiling of transcription and histone modifications in adult human brain regions to map cell-type-specific regulatory landscapes, developmental epigenetic memory, and neurological variant interpretation. The research establishes a framework for understanding human brain cell identity, evolution, and pathology.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cell-type-specific regulatory landscapes identified through transcription and histone modification profiling",
    "Developmental epigenetic memory patterns observed in brain regions",
    "Improved interpretation of neurological variants via multiomic data integration"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell multiomic profiling",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational framework for understanding human brain cell identity, evolution, and pathology through integrated single-cell multiomic analysis of transcription and hist: modifications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study designed dichalcogenide-hybrid mesoporous silica nanoparticles as GPX-mimetic nanozymes to address cytotoxicity and selectivity issues in existing systems. Structure-activity analysis revealed that chalcogen composition, density, and spatial proximity govern catalytic activity. The diselenide-hybrid framework showed superior performance in detoxifying peroxides, reducing liver injury in acetaminophen and rifampic as well as MASLD models, and improving survival without significant toxicity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Diselenide-hybrid mesoporous silica nanoparticles demonstrated highest GPX-like activity among tested materials",
    "The nanozymes effectively detoxified peroxides and reduced oxidative stress in liver injury models",
    "The material improved survival and alleviated steatosis in metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes dichalcogenide-hybrid frameworks as a tunable, non-toxic platform for GPX-mimetic catalysis, advancing strategies for oxidative stress-related liver disease treatment without metal dependency."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the design of a piezoelectric nanozyme heterojunction (BaTiO3@MIL-100(Fe,Cu)) to enhance cancer therapy through synergistic piezoelectric catalytic therapy (PCT) and nanozyme catalytic therapy (NCT). By engineering Cu2+ into MIL-100(Fe), the heterojunction achieved flexible energy band tuning, improving electron-hole separation and dual-enzyme activity. The system synergistically activated ferroptosis/cuproptosis pathways and modulated the tumor immune microenvironment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cu2+ engineering in MIL-100(Fe) altered charge transfer pathways and enhanced dual-enzyme activity",
    "Lattice distortion modulated the valence band gap, converting heterojunction from type-I to type-S for improved electron-hole separation",
    "The heterojunction synergistically activated ferroptosis/cuproptosis pathways and modulated the immunosuppressive tumor microenvironment"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a strategy for energy band tunable piezoelectric nanozyme heterojunctions that enhances dual catalytic therapy efficacy and tumor microenvironment modulation through precise electronic structure engineering."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates conserved striatal mechanisms in autism spectrum disorder (ASD) using a cross-species approach. Yuan et al. identified alterations in specific striatal neurons and astrocytes, revealing potential cellular and molecular pathways underlying striatal dysfunction in ASD.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Alterations in specific striatal neurons",
    "Alterations in specific stri: astrocytes",
    "Cross-species identification of striatal changes relevant to ASD"
  ],
  "study_type": "Cross-species approach",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide conserved cellular and molecular insights into striatal dysfunction mechanisms in ASD, advancing understanding of neurobiological underpinnings of social and stereotypic behaviors."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the photocatalytic upcycling of recalcitrant polyvinylidene fluoride (PVDF) plastic waste using Fe and Cu dual single atoms on In2P3S9 nanosheets. The researchers synthesized a photocatalyst achieving ∼1351.8 µmol g-. The approach involved in situ characterizations to confirm electron transfer mechanisms. The results demonstrate efficient conversion of raw PVDF to acetic/formic acid via photoexcited electrons and hydroxyl radicals under ambient conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fe and Cu dual single atoms on In2P3S9 nanosheets enable efficient photocatalytic conversion of raw PVDF plastic",
    "The best-performing catalyst (Fe1.0Cu0.5) generates ∼1351.8 µmol g-1 of acetic/formic acid",
    "In situ characterizations confirm electron transfer from In2P3S9 to Fe/Cu DSAs, with hydroxyl radicals driving PVDF upcycling"
  ],
  "study_type": "Photocatalysis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a sustainable pathway for converting highly resistant PVDF plastic waste into high-value chemicals using dual single-atom photocatalysts, addressing a critical challenge in plastic recycling."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates heptamethine cyanines as photocaged Michael electrophiles for targeted GPX4 inhibition and ferroptosis induction. Using photoactivation, the researchers achieved spatiotemporal control over GPX4 inhibition with high potency against cancer cells, including drug-resistant variants. The approach circumvented glutathione detoxification by selectively alkylating GP. The findings demonstrate a novel strategy for cancer immunotherapy via ferroptosis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Heptamethine cyanines function as photocaged Michael electrophiles enabling spatiotemporal GPX4 inhibition",
    "The photo-uncaged electrophiles selectively alkylate GPX4 selenocysteine over glutathione, bypassing cellular GSH detoxification",
    "Cy7 prodrugs selectively killed cancer cells in tumors under photoirradiation and induced systemic antitumor immunity"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a new paradigm for GPX4 inhibitor development by repurposing conventional cyanine dyes as photocaged therapeutics, enabling precise spatiotemporal control over ferroptosis induction and systemic antitumor immunity."
}

{
  "summary": "The study developed a cross-species atlas of the basal ganglia using single-cell transcriptomics and integrated multi-omic data to create a standardized framework for classifying brain cell types across human, macaque, marmoset, and mouse. This resource provides a curated taxonomy with phenotypic characterization and species-specific anatomical mapping, demonstrating scalable standards for building a comprehensive mammalian brain cell atlas.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Integrated single-cell transcriptomic classification with epigenomic, spatial genomic, and multiomic datasets",
    "Species-specific anatomical mapping of basal ganglia cell types with cross-species linkage via structural ontologies",
    "Established standardized pipelines for tissue acquisition, data processing, and interoperable metadata to enable whole-brain atlas development"
  ],
  "study_type": "Cross-species multimodal atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable framework for standardized, cross-species brain cell classification that advances the development of a comprehensive mammalian brain cell atlas through harmonized data integration and community-informed annotation."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines sodium-metal batteries (SMBs), highlighting the critical role of the solid-electrolyte interphase (SEI) in addressing performance bottlenecks. It systematically reviews electrolyte strategies to form mechanically robust, ion-conductive SEI layers and discusses in-situ/operando characterization techniques for understanding interfacial dynamics. Key findings include solvent engineering, salt chemistry optimization, and additive utilization for SEI modulation, with implications for enhancing Coulombic efficiency and mitigating dendrite growth.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Electrolyte strategies like solvent engineering and additive utilization modulate SEI formation for mechanical robustness",
    "In-situ/oper:operando characterization techniques reveal dynamic interfacial evolution during SMB operation",
    "Optimized SEI layers improve Coulombic efficiency and reduce dendrite growth risks"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a comprehensive framework for designing stable sodium-metal batteries by elucidating SEI formation mechanisms and electrolyte engineering strategies, advancing the field toward practical energy storage solutions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed charge-neutralized hydrogels using LiCl to suppress swelling and enhance stability, enabling tunable mechanical properties and 3D-printed curved structures. The system integrates curvature topography with mechanical loading to mimic soft tissue microenvironments, demonstrating effects on surfactant secretion, cell proliferation, and drug sensitivity in a microphysiological platform.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Charge-neutralization with LiCl suppresses hydrogel swelling by mitigating the Donnan effect",
    "Hydrogels exhibit tunable Young's modulus (1.12–339.79 kPa) and stable 3D-printed curved structures",
    "Curvature topography and mechanical loading influence tissue-specific phenotypes like surfactant secretion and drug sensitivity"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro microphysiological system",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a generalizable platform for reconstructing physiologically relevant soft tissue microenvironments by coupling curvature topography with mechanical cues."
}

{
  "summary": "This study created a cross-species multiomic atlas of primate basal ganglia using 1.8 million nuclei from humans, macauses, and marmosets across eight structures. It identified 61 homologous cell types conserved over 76 million years, revealing dorsal-ventral spatial identity as more conserved than receptor or striosome/matrix features. The atlas links psychiatric and neurodegenerative disease risk to specific cell populations and provides tools for viral targeting.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of 61 homologous cell types conserved across 76 million years in primates",
    "Dorsal-ventral spatial identity shows greater conservation than D1/D2 receptor or striosome/matrix identity",
    "Striatum D2 spiny projection neurons have distinct molecular, electrophysiological, and morphological features"
  ],
  "study_type": "Multiomic consensus atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a foundational resource for understanding basal ganglia evolution, function, and disease mechanisms across primates by integrating cross-species molecular and spatial data."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the design of healable thermoset elastomeric materials for passive radiative cooling (PRC). By integrating physical interactions and dynamic covalent bonds in a cross-linked network, the researchers created scalable PRC films with strong solar reflectance and long-wave infrared emittance. These materials maintain cooling efficiency after physical damage and healing, demonstrating dual functionality for summer roof cooling and winter ice preservation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Thermoset elastomeric PRC films exhibit self-healing capabilities after physical damage",
    "The materials maintain efficient cooling performance through both summer roof applications and winter ice preservation",
    "Scalable synthesis enables robust, extensible PRC films with tunable properties via inorganic coating and hierarchical architectures"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro synthesis and characterization",
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances PRC material design by enabling mechanically robust, healable, and scalable thermoset elastomers that overcome previous limitations in dimensional stability and longevity for practical thermal management applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how biomimetic hierarchical scaffolds influence mesenchymal stem cells (MSCs) and Schwann cells (SCs) interactions for bone regeneration. Using a rabbit bone defect model, the researchers designed multi-channel scaffolds that enhanced MSC/SC crosstalk, leading to 3.24-fold increased bone regeneration and 2.29-fold improved neuro-vascular networks compared to traditional scaffolds. The findings highlight the role of spatially organized scaffolds in orchestrating multicellular interactions for tissue repair.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Hierarchical multi-channel scaffolds promoted MSC/SC mutual migration and energy metabolism",
    "Transcriptomic analysis identified cytokine-cytokine receptor-mediated cross-talk activating neurogenesis/osteogenesis pathways",
    "Rabbit model showed 3.24-fold greater bone regeneration and 2.29-fold enhanced neuro-vascular networks with the biomimetic scaffolds"
  ],
  "study_type": "Rabbit bone defect model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that spatially structured biomimetic scaffolds can enhance multicellular interactions to accelerate complex tissue regeneration, providing a novel strategy for engineering regenerative biomaterials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated a high-resolution spatial transcriptomics atlas of the basal ganglia across human, rhesus macaque, and common marmoset species, integrating it with cross-species single-nucleus RNA sequencing data. The atlas reveals stereotyped multi-axis gene expression gradients and core-shell organization within the internal globus pallidus, providing a foundational resource for understanding basal ganglia molecular organization in health and disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Extensive spatial sampling across the rostral-caudal axis reveals stereotyped multi-axis gene expression gradients in the striatum",
    "Identification of core-shell organization within the internal globus pallidus",
    "Cross-species comparison of basal ganglia molecular organization across three primate species"
  ],
  "study_type": "Spatial transcriptomics atlas with cross-species single-nucle: RNA sequencing integration",
  "scientific_significance": "This cross-species spatial transcriptomics atlas establishes a unified framework for understanding basal ganglia molecular organization across primates, advancing comparative neuroanatomy and disease mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and improves Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieved 1756.5 mAh g-1 capacity, 868.4 m. Ah g-1 at 3 C, and reduced thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles, demonstrating scalable performance in 6 kg batches for NCM811 batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doping enhances carbon interlayer spacing and electronic conductivity, improving Li+ insertion/extraction kinetics",
    "The composite achieved 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C with 13.1% thickness expansion after 50 cycles"
  ],
  "study_type": "Material design and synthesis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, addressing mechanical instability in high-energy lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered FGF2-functionalized adipose-derived mesenchymal stem cell extracellular vesicles (EV-FGF2) within an ECM-mimetic hydrogel to treat diabetic wounds. The approach enhanced macrophage polarization, neurovascular responses, and reduced scarring in animal models by leveraging sustained FGF2 release and hydrogel support. Results showed accelerated wound closure, decreased inflammation, and improved tissue remodeling without cellular components.",
  "key_findings": [
    "EV-FGF2 promoted macrophage polarization toward reparative M2 phenotype in vitro",
    "CH/EV-F:GF2 hydrogel accelerated wound closure and reduced inflammation in diabetic mouse models",
    "The system increased vascular (CD31) and neuronal (βIII-tubulin) markers while attenuating scar formation in rabbit ear models"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo animal models",
  "scientific_significance": "This engineered EV-FGF2 hydrogel system provides a cell-free strategy to simultaneously target inflammation, neurovascular dysfunction, and scar formation in diabetic wounds, advancing tissue repair mechanisms without cellular transplantation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used Slide-tags single-nucleus spatial transcriptomics to profile 1.1 million cells across 19 human postmortem donors, revealing six molecularly distinct striatal zones with spatially coordinated neuron-astrocyte interactions. A mouse atlas confirmed four homologous zones aligned with brain-wide afferent projections. The research found dorsal striatal zones show the strongest age-related transcriptional changes, with zonal molecular differences diminishing as aging progresses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Six molecularly distinct striatal zones defined by spiny projection neuron populations",
    "Spatially coordinated neuron-astrocyte interaction networks within each zone",
    "Dorsal striatal zones exhibit the greatest age-related transcriptional changes"
  ],
  "study_type": "Slide-tags single-nucleus spatial transcriptomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a conserved mesoscale spatial framework for the mammalian striatum, linking single-cell molecular identity to structural connectomics and aging processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates strategies to enhance aqueous manganese metal battery (AMMB) cycling stability by addressing hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) at the Mn anode. Using n-decyltrimethylammonium bromide (10-DTAB) as a surfactant with high LUMO energy, the researchers reconstructed the electric double layer to improve interfacial stability. The approach achieved a 93% Coulombic efficiency, indicating reduced HER and better cycling reversibility for AMMBs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "10-DTAB surfactant addition stabilized the Mn anode interface by reconstructing the electric double layer",
    "High LUMO energy of 1.0-DTAB enhanced reduction stability, preventing continuous decomposition",
    "The strategy achieved 93% Coulombic efficiency, significantly improving cycling reversibility"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro electrochemical study",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a general paradigm for stabilizing reactive metal anodes in aqueous batteries through electric double layer engineering, providing a foundational approach for durable manganese-based energy storage systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether bio-orthogonally functionalized biomimetic nanoreactors could suppress lung cancer stem-like cells (LCSCs) by disrupting ER-mitochondria crosstalk. Using an N-cadherin-targeting aptamer and tumor membrane masking, the nanoreactor delivered TAPP and bortez. Laser activation induced ROS, mitochondrial damage, and ER stress, triggering a self-amplifying stress loop that reduced LCSC survival via STAT3 inhibition and stemness markers. The approach demonstrates a targeted mechanism for LCSC elimination.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Laser-activated nanoreactors delivered TAPP and bortezomib to induce ROS and mitochondrial damage",
    "ER stress from bortezomib triggered Ca2+ release into mitochondria, exacerbating dysfunction",
    "The self-amplifying ER-mitochondria stress loop reduced LCSC survival via STAT3 inhibition and stemness marker downregulation"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro nanoreactor-based intervention",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a targeted strategy for disrupting protective ER-mitochondria crosstalk in LCSCs, providing a mechanism for selective elimination through self-amplifying stress induction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used single-nucleus RNA sequencing on 3.9 million nuclei from 178 adults to investigate inter-individual variation in the human striatum and prefrontal cortex. It found that astrocyte, microglia, and OPC proportions were consistently higher in brains with more of these cell types across gray matter regions, OPCs declined with age, and age could be predicted from gene expression with a median error of 6.6 years. The data also revealed cell-type-specific genetic variants influencing gene expression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Astrocyte, microglia, and oligodendrocyte precursor cell proportions were consistently elevated across gray matter regions in brains with higher counts in one region",
    "Oligodendrocyte precursor cell proportions decreased by 40% between ages 30-80 in both cortex and striatum",
    "Donor age could be predicted from RNA expression patterns with a median absolute error of 6.6 years across cell types"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-nucleus RNA sequencing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive atlas of cell-type-specific genetic variation and gene expression patterns in human striatum and prefrontal cortex, providing a foundational resource for understanding brain development, aging, and disease susceptibility."
}
